  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Cote D&#x2019;Ivoire 2025 &#x2013; IOM Hydraulic EngineerII</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM in C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire is actively engaged alongside the Ivorian government to support efforts for conflict prevention and peace promotion, while contributing to stability and security in border regions. Its programmes and activities combine access to basic social services, peacebuilding, and migration management, with a particular focus on preventing and managing conflicts related to natural resources. The Community Stabilization (CS) Unit is implementing several projects, with significant components focused on improving access to water, notably through the construction of multipurposehydraulic structures that address both domestic and livelihood needs. IOM also invests in developing knowledge products on water resources, particularly in northern C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire. At the same time, IOM plays a key role in strengthening Integrated Water Resources Management (IWRM), with a view to promoting effective planning, management, and conservation of these resources.</narrative>
  </description>
